          alt: "The painless eye and the painful eye — two of Ghana's leading causes of blindness. Cataract — clouding of the lens: painless, vision blurs over months or years, glare, colours fade, the pupil may look grey or white; reversible, surgery restores sight; the barrier in Ghana is reaching the operation — distance, cost, fear, the belief that failing sight is normal ageing. Glaucoma — pressure damaging the nerve: chronic form painless, takes the edges of vision first; acute form severe eye pain, headache, vomiting, red eye, haloes, hazy cornea, fixed mid-dilated pupil; not reversible; acute glaucoma is a same-hour emergency. The question at the door: does the eye hurt, and did the vision change suddenly? Gradual and painless can wait; sudden, painful, red or sudden loss of vision must be seen today, as must chemical splash, penetrating injury and a curtain across the vision. After eye surgery the danger is pressure and infection: do not rub, bend below the waist, lift heavy loads or strain at stool; report increasing pain, discharge or worsening vision at once.",
